.TH QFW-ACTIVATE 1 "August 2026" "QFw 0.1.0" "QFw Commands"
.SH NAME
qfw-activate \- prepare a shell to use an installed QFw environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B source prefix/bin/qfw-activate
.RI [ --venv " directory" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qfw-activate
must be sourced by Bash. It adds the selected QFw and DEFw installation to the
current shell, preserves the caller's previous environment, and defines the
.BR qfw-deactivate (1)
shell function.
.PP
Activation does not create an application run directory and does not start a
directory service, DVM, or QPM. Application runtime state is created later by
.BR qfw-setup (1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --venv " directory"
Activate the Python virtual environment at
.I directory
before adding QFw and DEFw paths. The environment must contain an executable
.IR bin/python
and a readable
.IR bin/activate .
The matching
.BR qfw-deactivate (1)
restores the Python environment that was active before this option was used.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Print usage. Because this command is sourced, help returns control to the
current shell.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B qfw-activate
sets installation-derived variables including
.BR QFW_PREFIX ,
.BR QFW_BIN_PATH ,
.BR QFW_LIBEXEC_DIR ,
.BR QFW_SHARE_DIR ,
.BR QFW_SITE_CONFIG ,
.BR DEFW_PREFIX ,
.BR DEFW_PATH ,
and
.BR DEFW_CONFIG_PATH .
It updates
.BR PATH ,
.BR PYTHONPATH ,
.BR LD_LIBRARY_PATH ,
and
.B MANPATH
without discarding existing values.
.PP
If
.B QFW_RUN_BASE_DIR
is already set, activation preserves it. Application launchers set this value
to shared storage before
.B qfw-setup
when a multinode runtime needs a common path.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Sourcing returns zero on success. Invalid options, a missing virtual
environment, or direct execution return nonzero.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qfw-deactivate (1),
.BR qfw-setup (1),
.BR qfw-status (1),
.BR qfw (7)
